# seq4h button map for the Anbernic RG40XX-V under Knulli.
# Copy next to the seq4h binary, replacing any older copy. Each line:
# SOURCE CODE BUTTON. Later lines win.
# Buttons: up down left right a b x y l r l2 r2 select start menu page roll undo lock quit prev next none
# To see the code each button sends: M > BUTTON CODES, or SHOW-BUTTONS in Ports.

# Read the pad as a raw joystick. Some H700 pads report a GUID that SDL
# mistakes for another controller, which would scramble the buttons.
mode joystick

# Raw button codes of the RG40XX-V pad under Knulli ("Deeplay-keys").
# joy 1 and joy 2 are volume down/up; Knulli handles them.
joy 3  a
joy 4  b
joy 5  y
joy 6  x
joy 7  l          # L1
joy 8  r          # R1
joy 9  select
joy 10 start
joy 11 menu       # M: main menu
joy 13 l2         # L2: previous track
joy 14 r2         # R2: next track
# The analog stick, left / right: previous / next step on every page. If
# BUTTON CODES shows another axis number for the stick, change the 0.
axis 0- prev
axis 0+ next
# joy 12 is the stick press.
# joy 12 undo     # example: stick press undoes the last roll

# Anbernic's stock firmware numbers the buttons 3 lower. If your codes look
# like that (check with BUTTON CODES), use these lines instead of the ones above:
# joy 0 a
# joy 1 b
# joy 2 y
# joy 3 x
# joy 4 l
# joy 5 r
# joy 6 select
# joy 7 start
# joy 13 menu
# joy 10 l2
# joy 11 r2
# (and set joy 8, joy 9 and joy 14 to none)

# The D-pad is hat 0.
hat up    up
hat down  down
hat left  left
hat right right

# The left stick can drive the cursor too (axes 0 and 1):
# axis 0- left
# axis 0+ right
# axis 1- up
# axis 1+ down
